text:
samir: FYI — customer FinLedger reporting structured JSON mode failures on /v1/generate. App gets a 422 and downstream parser crash. request_id=abc123 model=rwd-open-2 mode=json_schema
lia: Can you paste the raw request body + the error payload from our logs? Also their SDK version?
samir: SDK 1.4.2. Here's the body we received (redacted):
```json
{
  "prompt": "invoice extraction",
  "structured_output": {
    "schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "invoices": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": ["id","amount","date"],
            "properties": {
              "id": {"type":"string"},
              "amount": {"type":"number"},
              "date": {"type":"string"},
              "lines": {"type":"array"}
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
samir: Response (trimmed):
```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "InvalidStructuredOutput",
    "message": "validation failed: invoices[2] missing required field 'amount'",
    "request_id": "abc123"
  }
}
```
ops-bot: [automated] 422 InvalidStructuredOutput request_id=abc123 path=/v1/generate duration=342ms node=host-12 region=us-west-2
mike: Did the model actually drop the field or did our post-processor strip it? Need raw token-level output. Also customer mentioned extra keys like `internal_note` inside invoice objects — that shouldn't break strict validation but will if validation forbids additionalProperties.
lia: Repro steps from customer: they POST the same body, sometimes get valid JSON, sometimes get the 422. They said failures increase with >12 items in invoices array. They suspect ordering/streaming edge.
oncall-ml: @eng-runtime can you look at streaming validator? Hypothesis: chunk boundary landed inside an object and our incremental parser treated it as truncated object and then validating against schema saw missing required fields.
eng-runtime: Investigating — the validator has two modes: validation_mode=strict (default) rejects extraProperties and missing required fields; in streaming path we reconstitute fragments but there was a race when array items arrived across multiple data frames. We'll reproduce.
samir: Customer also flagged billing: they were billed for 3 retries because SDK resent on parse failure. They asked for credits.
lia: Steps to repro locally: 1) run a loop to request with invoices array length 15. 2) throttle network to 100ms chunking (e.g., tc qdisc/netem) 3) use mode=json_schema and validation_mode=strict 4) observe occasional 422. Example curl: 
```bash
curl -X POST "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '@payload.json'
```
(where payload.json is the body above with a long invoices list)
mike: On my repro I saw this stack in logs: `validator_stream.go:214 validateChunk -> eofDuringObject -> emitInvalidStructuredOutput`. I also saw extra property `internal_note` present in some items. If additionalProperties is false in schema, that will cause rejections. But the root cause seems to be fragmentation not schema itself.
oncall-ml: Proposed interim mitigation: set validation_mode=lenient for hosted customers so we accept extra keys and missing optional fields (log a warning and attach a validation_report). Then apply a robust assembler that buffers full JSON objects before running full-schema validation.
eng-runtime: Agreed. We'll ship two changes: 1) streaming assembler: ensure we only run JSON schema validation on a complete object/array item boundary. 2) change default for hosted to lenient for any request using streaming=true while we ramp. Patch PR: https://git.internal/rw/eng-runtime/pulls/452 (rolling to canary now).
lia: Customer relief: offer to credit the extra retries and give them the canary toggle to opt into lenient mode.
samir: Customer accepted credit + will try canary. Provided them a temporary flag: `X-Redwood-Feature: lenient_json_mode=true`
eng-runtime: Can confirm canary deployed to us-west-2. Monitoring: validation_failures for json_schema down 95% for affected endpoints. Patch also appends a `validation_report` field to metadata with warnings.
ops-bot: [automated] deployment canary -> us-west-2 pr=452 status=success duration=6m
mike: Follow-ups: 1) Add explicit docs note about ordering assumptions in arrays — schemas shouldn't rely on model preserving order unless specified. 2) Add rate/billing guard so we don't bill for automatic retries caused by server-side parse failures.
lia: Filed a billing ticket: billing/credit request for FinLedger, refs: BL-789. Support to process credit once eng-runtime confirms resolution.
samir: Marking this resolved for now. Will reopen if customer sees recurrence after canary. Thanks everyone. :tada:
